{# horizontal_process treatment (A3-landscape, archetype "process").

   REBUILT 2026-07-13 to the ST-06 reference spread anatomy (a published
   mechanism spread; a sibling spread confirms the family): NOT a row of flat
   cards on a spine, but a THREE-ZONE spread:

     LEFT  : the PRODUCT MOCKUP as the hero visual (the client's real pre-framed
             device render), then the centered two-tone headline and the lede
             (einleitung) beneath it.
     MIDDLE: the NAVY NUMBERED-STEPS PANEL (Richard's signature device: a dark
             rounded panel, oversized accent numerals 01..NN inline with a bold
             on-dark title, the step body in on-dark text).
     RIGHT : a FULL-HEIGHT navy rail carrying the payoff statement (td.result,
             the mechanism's closing line) as a large on-dark serif statement,
             and the CTA (label + brand URL) anchored at the rail foot.

   Driven entirely by TreatmentData; every zone graceful-omits (no mockup ->
   the left zone is headline+lede only; no result -> the rail leads with the
   CTA). Token-only styling in styles/treatments/horizontal_process.css. #}
{% from 'eyebrow.jinja' import eyebrow %}
{% from 'two_tone_headline.jinja' import two_tone_headline %}
{% from 'viz.jinja' import viz as render_viz %}

{% set hp_lede = (td.body[0] if td.body else none) or td.subhead %}
{% set _brand_url = (ctx.brand.company_url_display if (ctx and ctx.brand) else '') or '' %}

<div class="hp-grid">

  {# ---- LEFT: mockup hero + headline + lede ---- #}
  <div class="hp-left">
    {% if td.images %}
    <img class="hp-hero-mockup" src="{{ td.images[0] }}" alt=""/>
    {% endif %}
    <div class="hp-head">
      {% if td.eyebrow %}{{ eyebrow(td.eyebrow) }}{% endif %}
      {% if td.headline %}
        {{ two_tone_headline(td.headline, td.headline_accent or '', tag='h1') }}
      {% endif %}
      {% if hp_lede %}<p class="hp-lede">{{ hp_lede }}</p>{% endif %}
    </div>
    {# generated SVG components (the ST-06 process-flow device) render as a band
       under the lede, sized to the left column width. Graceful: only when
       td.components is non-empty. US-2026-08-25 (the p20 crew): on the ST-06
       MECHANISM showcase the middle navy numbered-steps panel IS the process
       device; re-rendering the orphan flow SVG as a second band under the lede
       duplicates the 6-step visual (the "no thought" double-viz the reviewer
       hammered). Suppress the component band for the mechanism role — one
       device, not two. #}
    {% if td.components and td.page_role != 'mechanism' %}
    <div class="hp-comps">
      {% for c in td.components %}<div class="hp-comp">{{ c | safe }}</div>{% endfor %}
    </div>
    {% endif %}
    {# any data-viz devices (gauge/donut/arrow) close the left zone #}
    {% if td.viz %}
    <div class="hp-viz">{{ render_viz(td.viz) }}</div>
    {% endif %}
  </div>

  {# ---- MIDDLE: the navy numbered-steps panel ---- #}
  {% if td.steps %}
  <div class="hp-steps-panel{% if td.page_role == 'mechanism' %} is-mechanism{% endif %}">
    {% for s in td.steps %}
    <div class="hp-step">
      <span class="hp-step-n">{{ '%02d' | format(loop.index) }}</span>
      <div class="hp-step-text">
        {% if s.title %}<span class="hp-step-title">{{ s.title }}</span>{% endif %}
        {% if s.body %}<span class="hp-step-body">{{ s.body }}</span>{% endif %}
      </div>
    </div>
    {% endfor %}
  </div>
  {% endif %}

  {# ---- RIGHT: navy payoff + CTA rail. The "Ergebnis" cap belongs to the payoff:
     both render only when td.result carries text; without it the rail is
     CTA-only and the modifier class centers the CTA vertically. ---- #}
  {% set _has_result = td.result and td.result.text %}
  <div class="hp-rail{% if not _has_result %} hp-rail--cta-only{% endif %}">
    {% if _has_result %}
    <div class="hp-rail-cap">Ergebnis</div>
    <div class="hp-rail-payoff">
      <p class="hp-rail-statement">{{ td.result.text }}</p>
      {% if td.result.source %}<div class="hp-rail-source">{{ td.result.source }}</div>{% endif %}
    </div>
    {% endif %}
    {% if _brand_url %}
    <div class="hp-rail-cta">
      <span class="hp-rail-cta-label">{{ (td.cta.text if td.cta else none) or 'Jetzt Termin vereinbaren' }}</span>
      <span class="hp-rail-cta-url">{{ _brand_url }}</span>
    </div>
    {% endif %}
  </div>

</div>
